                      (ruction_runtime.s):00596         ; DOC-002 source-contract mirror begins. Canonical definitions:
                      (ruction_runtime.s):00597         ; wiki/internal/implementation/routine-catalog.html
                      (ruction_runtime.s):00598         ; DOC-002 source-contract mirror profile copy Inputs: Source and destination identities, bounded count or stream metadata, and any required mapped page
                      (ruction_runtime.s):00599         ; DOC-002 source-contract mirror profile copy Outputs: Copied, decoded, merged, cached, or addressed data plus caller-visible pointer progress
                      (ruction_runtime.s):00600         ; DOC-002 source-contract mirror profile copy Clobbers: A, B, D, X, Y, U, and condition codes unless a narrower source-local header is present
                      (ruction_runtime.s):00601         ; DOC-002 source-contract mirror profile copy Reads: The declared source stream, table, framebuffer rows, or metadata record
                      (ruction_runtime.s):00602         ; DOC-002 source-contract mirror profile copy Writes: Only the declared bounded destination record, cache, row range, or scratch fields
                      (ruction_runtime.s):00603         ; DOC-002 source-contract mirror profile copy Side effects: May temporarily map a required GIME page while moving or decoding data
                      (ruction_runtime.s):00604         ; DOC-002 source-contract mirror profile copy Invariants: Counts and destination bounds are honored; any temporary GIME mapping is restored before returning unless the routine contract explicitly states otherwise
                      (ruction_runtime.s):00605         ; DOC-002 source-contract mirror profile presentation Inputs: Presentation state, interval timer, input edges, current map, and the selected auxiliary profile
                      (ruction_runtime.s):00606         ; DOC-002 source-contract mirror profile presentation Outputs: Updated presentation state and the dispatcher retain/release status when applicable
                      (ruction_runtime.s):00607         ; DOC-002 source-contract mirror profile presentation Clobbers: A, B, D, X, Y, U, and condition codes unless a narrower source-local header is present
                      (ruction_runtime.s):00608         ; DOC-002 source-contract mirror profile presentation Reads: Presentation direct-page state, cold payloads, authored map streams, and input state
                      (ruction_runtime.s):00609         ; DOC-002 source-contract mirror profile presentation Writes: Presentation state, mapped BACK pixels, and presentation-owned persistent metadata
                      (ruction_runtime.s):00610         ; DOC-002 source-contract mirror profile presentation Side effects: May retain the foreground interval or produce a complete presentation surface
                      (ruction_runtime.s):00611         ; DOC-002 source-contract mirror profile presentation Invariants: Gameplay simulation begins only after release; hidden hydration may prepare initial-stage state and hold it unchanged until release; FRONT publication remains IRQ-owned
                      (ruction_runtime.s):00612         ; DOC-002 source-contract mirror profile render Inputs: Current render intent, selected actor or tile state, and a valid BACK or staging destination
                      (ruction_runtime.s):00613         ; DOC-002 source-contract mirror profile render Outputs: Updated destination pixels and any owner-local history required by later restoration
                      (ruction_runtime.s):00614         ; DOC-002 source-contract mirror profile render Clobbers: A, B, D, X, Y, U, and condition codes unless a narrower source-local header is present
                      (ruction_runtime.s):00615         ; DOC-002 source-contract mirror profile render Reads: Authoritative gameplay state, immutable art streams, and current owner-local background metadata
                      (ruction_runtime.s):00616         ; DOC-002 source-contract mirror profile render Writes: BACK or staging pixels, render scratch, and owner-local save-under or damage metadata
                      (ruction_runtime.s):00617         ; DOC-002 source-contract mirror profile render Side effects: Changes a non-visible composition surface or its metadata
                      (ruction_runtime.s):00618         ; DOC-002 source-contract mirror profile render Invariants: The routine never selects the visible FRONT surface; temporary PAR5 mappings expire or restore before return
